<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Tefilas HaMinchah [Laws of the Afternoon Prayer]<br>Halachah 6 (§§ 1–13)<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">Based on <span class="lr">LM II:71</span> (<i>Chavalim Naflu Li BaN'imim</i>)</span></div>

<div class="sn">Introduction — The <i>No'am</i>, <i>Kavod</i>, <i>Chovlim</i> and <i>N'imim</i></div>

<div class="p">Based on the teaching "<span class="h">Chavalim Naflu Li BaN'imim</span>" (<span class="lr">LM II:71</span>). See there.</div>

<div class="p">The principle: all of Creation is solely for His glory [<span class="h">kavod</span>]. Therefore <span class="h">kavod</span> is the root of all Creation — the root of all the Ten Utterances by which the world was created. When honor comes to a person, he must be very careful not to take any of it for himself — he must elevate all the <span class="h">kavod</span> to Hashem. He must understand from which Utterance this <span class="h">kavod</span> was generated. The essential <span class="h">kavod</span> is through man (= the purpose of all Creation), who was created to magnify and publicize His <span class="h">kavod</span>. Through procreation [<span class="h">holadah</span>] — more people being born — His <span class="h">kavod</span> is revealed further. The essential <span class="h">holadah</span> is through the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> [the Supernal Pleasantness], the supreme root of procreation. The <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> flows constantly, but a vessel [<span class="h">k'li</span>] is needed to receive it — made through <span class="h">tzedakah</span> (to receive the flames of love flowing from the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>). There is <span class="h">tzedakah</span> of Eretz Yisrael and <span class="h">tzedakah</span> of outside the Land. The essential one is the <span class="h">tzedakah</span> of Eretz Yisrael — the <span class="h">mochin</span> of Eretz Yisrael are in the aspect of <span class="h">no'am</span>: <span class="mx">"they delight each other in <i>halachah</i>"</span> (= <span class="h">shalom</span>). Outside the Land is the aspect of <span class="h">chovlim</span> [those who wound/injure] — the <span class="h">mochin</span> of outside the Land are <span class="h">machaloikes</span> [dispute]: <span class="mx">"they wound each other in <i>halachah</i>."</span></div>

<div class="p">When the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> flows (for <span class="h">holadah</span> through the vessel of <span class="h">tzedakah</span>), the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (= <span class="h">mochin</span> of outside the Land) fall into the <span class="h">n'imim</span> [the pleasant ones] (= <span class="h">mochin</span> of Eretz Yisrael) to be repaired (that being their time of tikun — their essential corruption came through flawed <span class="h">kavod</span>). But sometimes the <span class="h">chovlim</span> are so damaged they cannot be repaired — rather, they cause damage to the <span class="h">n'imim</span> as well. From this comes the <span class="h">machaloikes</span> that exists even in Eretz Yisrael. The <span class="h">n'imim</span> themselves are the aspect of <span class="h">shalom</span> — dispute comes only from the damaged <span class="h">chovlim</span> falling among them, and when too corrupt, they damage the <span class="h">n'imim</span>. All through flawed <span class="h">kavod</span> — all the <span class="h">machaloikes</span> in the world, in Eretz Yisrael and outside, derives from there.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 1 — Three Daily <i>Tefilos</i>: Drawing the <i>No'am</i>; <i>Tefilah</i> as the Essential <i>Kavod</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the three daily <span class="h">tefilos</span>. The <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> must be drawn each day: <span class="mx">"in His goodness He renews the act of Creation every day."</span> The essential Creation was through the <span class="h">No'am</span> — revealing His <span class="h">kavod</span> (= the root of Creation). Every day, renewed Creation comes through the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> flowing, drawing Jewish souls — magnifying His <span class="h">kavod</span>, sustaining the world. The world's essential sustenance is through <span class="h">tzedakah</span> and <span class="h">chesed</span> (our Sages say) — <span class="h">tzedakah</span> creates the vessel to receive the <span class="h">No'am</span>, revealing His <span class="h">kavod</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Daylight is the essential renewed Creation: Hashem causes the sun to rise each morning and set in the evening. We praise this in <span class="h">Birchos HaMe'oros</span>: <span class="mx">"in His goodness He renews the act of Creation every day."</span> Daylight is the radiance of the <span class="h">kavod</span>: <span class="v">"the earth shone from His <i>kavod</i>"</span> — drawn from the <span class="h">mochin</span> of the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>: <span class="v">"sweet [<i>masok</i>] is the light"</span> (= pleasantness and sweetness). The <span class="h">mochin</span> are the aspect of daylight: <span class="v">"wisdom's advantage... as the advantage of light over darkness."</span> The essential <span class="h">No'am</span> flows in the morning (= daylight). This is <span class="h">Shacharis</span> established by Avraham — the first to reveal His G-dliness: <span class="mx">"These are the generations of the heavens and the earth — <i>b'hibaram</i> / <i>b'Avraham</i>"</span> (our Sages). Avraham began drawing the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> (= the holy <span class="h">mochin</span> of Eretz Yisrael) — the essential knowledge of His G-dliness. He engaged in <span class="h">tzedakah</span> and <span class="h">chesed</span> all his days to create the vessel. <span class="h">No'am</span> = the right side, Avraham: <span class="v">"pleasantness at Your right hand forever."</span> He was first to reveal the holiness of Eretz Yisrael (meriting its <span class="h">mochin</span> of <span class="h">no'am</span>). Therefore Avraham established <span class="h">Shacharis</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The complete order of prayer is in the morning: <span class="h">Pesukay D'Zimrah</span> (= <span class="v">"pleasant songster of Israel"</span> — drawing the <span class="h">No'am</span>); preceded by <span class="h">parshas haKorbanos</span> (= <span class="h">tzedakah</span>, generous heart — receiving the <span class="h">No'am</span>); then <span class="h">Birchos HaMe'oros</span> and <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> (= drawing the <span class="h">mochin</span>); then <span class="h">Shemoneh Esrai</span> (= drawing the souls, the <span class="h">mochin</span> further below).</div>

<div class="p">Through all this, His <span class="h">kavod</span> is revealed. The essential <span class="h">kavod</span> is through <span class="h">tefilah</span> specifically — when we pray and ask for all our needs, physical and spiritual: <span class="v">"call upon Me in the day of trouble; I shall deliver you, and you shall honor Me."</span> This is the essential <span class="h">kavod</span>. <span class="h">Shemoneh Esrai</span> is higher and more precious than the entire order of prayer — through prayer we demonstrate that Hashem governs the world, watches over every detail, and has the power to change nature. He gave us the power and permission to entreat Him through prayer and supplication — until He turns from judgment to mercy, nullifying all unfavorable decrees and filling all our needs. This is the completeness of His <span class="h">kavod</span>: as long as this is not made known, His <span class="h">kavod</span> is not yet fully revealed. Praising Him and acknowledging His greatness is <span class="h">kavod</span>, but the completeness is declaring that He still watches over His world now, overriding His will for the will of Israel when they increase in prayer — this is why He created everything. As explained in the teaching "<span class="h">Elokim Al D'mi Lach</span>" (<span class="lr">LM I:97</span>): the essential Creation was because He foresaw receiving delight from Israel who would rule through their prayers.</div>

<div class="p">This wondrous thing — creating man with free will who has the power, as it were, to rule over Him — is exceedingly remote from human intellect. But these are His mighty deeds: the essential magnification of His <span class="h">kavod</span> is when we acknowledge all these things far from our understanding, yet believe in His greatness whose thoughts and ways are immeasurably higher than ours. This path of <span class="h">tefilah</span> our forefathers revealed — beginning with Avraham, who labored enormously, broke all his cravings, devoted himself in prayer and supplication until he drew the path of <span class="h">tefilah</span> into the world: <span class="h">Shacharis</span>. Then Yitzchak and Yaakov established further: <span class="h">Minchah</span> and <span class="h">Arvis</span>. All the true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> after them until today followed their path, strengthening us to increase in prayer. We must nullify our deficient understanding and follow our forefathers' way — increasing in <span class="h">tefilah</span> for everything, believing we have the power to "defeat" Him, turning judgment to mercy — though we cannot understand it. This is the essential completeness of His <span class="h">kavod</span> — through <span class="h">tefilah</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 2 — After Midday: The <i>Chovlim</i> Rise; the Golden Calf; Yitzchak Established <i>Minchah</i></div>

<div class="p">The essential <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> (= the <span class="h">mochin</span> of Eretz Yisrael) flows at <span class="h">Shacharis</span>. Day brightens until noon. After midday, daylight diminishes — the <span class="h">No'am</span> (= <span class="h">mochin</span>) contracts. Then the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (= <span class="h">mochin</span> of outside the Land = <span class="h">machaloikes</span>) seek to overpower. Their sustenance comes when the light of the <span class="h">no'am</span> diminishes — when the <span class="h">mochin</span> are complete, no doubt, dispute, or <span class="h">chovlim</span> can exist. Only when the <span class="h">mochin</span> begin diminishing (= after midday) do doubts, difficulties, and <span class="h">machaloikes</span> (= <span class="h">chovlim</span>) take hold. Without repair — all corruption and flaws result.</div>

<div class="p">This is the sin of the Golden Calf through the <span class="h">Erev Rav</span> — after midday specifically: <span class="v">"the people saw — <i>ki ba sheish</i>"</span> (our Sages: "the sixth hour arrived"). The <span class="h">Erev Rav</span> are <span class="h">machaloikes</span> — sustenance from <span class="h">chovlim</span>, the most damaged <span class="h">mochin</span> of outside the Land (from Egypt — the ultimate contamination of outside the Land). They needed repair through the <span class="h">no'am</span> of the <span class="h">mochin</span> drawn at Sinai (the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>: <span class="v">"her ways are ways of pleasantness, and all her paths are peace"</span>). But being so terribly damaged, not only were they not repaired, they also damaged the <span class="h">n'imim</span> — misleading Israel into the great sin of the Calf. All after midday specifically.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Yitzchak established <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> (after midday) — to sweeten the <span class="h">chovlim</span>, preventing them from damaging the <span class="h">n'imim</span>. Yitzchak specifically — as the first holy birth in Israel (the essential magnification of His <span class="h">kavod</span>). The essential <span class="h">kavod</span> is through <span class="h">holadah</span> — Yitzchak being the first born in Israel's holiness. When Avraham began drawing holiness, he himself was not yet born in that holiness — Yitzchak was the first. Then all the <span class="h">chovlim</span> come to be repaired (especially at this first holy birth). Yitzchak therefore was the intensity of judgment — the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (= judgments) seeking to take hold in him. He established <span class="h">Minchah</span> (after midday, where <span class="h">chovlim</span> begin) — needing most to repair the <span class="h">chovlim</span> that come with the holy birth.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 3 — Extra Caution at <i>Minchah</i>: <i>Chovlim</i> Confuse Prayer; Eliyahu</div>

<div class="p">The Sages warned to be exceedingly careful with <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> — the <span class="h">chovlim</span> must then be repaired, and this is the essential tikun of <span class="h">tefilah</span>. The <span class="h">chovlim</span> confuse thought in prayer: every <span class="h">tefilah</span> draws <span class="h">mochin</span> from the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>, generating souls (= <span class="h">holadah</span>), magnifying His <span class="h">kavod</span>. As soon as one stands to pray, the <span class="h">chovlim</span> come to be repaired — and from the great flaws clinging to them (especially in these generations), they damage the <span class="h">n'imim</span> and confuse thought terribly. One must overpower them greatly — especially at <span class="h">Minchah</span> when <span class="mx">"harsh judgment prevails"</span> (Zohar) — their essential sustenance being then, and <span class="h">Minchah</span>'s essential purpose being to sweeten them. One must pray <span class="h">Minchah</span> with intense <span class="h">kavanah</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"One should always be careful with <i>Tefilas HaMinchah</i>, for Eliyahu was answered only at <i>Minchah</i>."</span> Eliyahu needed to nullify the idolatry derived from the <span class="h">chovlim</span>'s damage (= <span class="h">machaloikes</span>; through <span class="h">machaloikes</span> one comes to idolatry [<span class="lr">LM I:251</span>]). <span class="v">"How long will you hobble on two opinions?"</span> — the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (= <span class="h">machaloikes</span> and doubts). Their subduing was at <span class="h">Minchah</span> specifically. <span class="v">"All the people saw, fell on their faces, and said: 'Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>.'"</span> <span class="v">"They fell on their faces"</span> = <span class="v">"the <i>chovlim</i> fell among the <i>n'imim</i>"</span> — the people in whom the <span class="h">chovlim</span> had taken hold (leading to idolatry) now fell upon the <span class="h">n'imim</span> (= their true face; <span class="v">"seven joys before Your face, pleasantness at Your right hand"</span> — the holy <span class="h">mochin</span> of <span class="h">no'am</span>). They were truly repaired. <span class="v">"Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>"</span> twice — <span class="h">chovlim</span> draw from judgment (<span class="h">Elokim</span>), <span class="h">n'imim</span> from mercy (Hashem). Now: judgment encompassed by mercy, <span class="h">chovlim</span> encompassed by <span class="h">n'imim</span>. Said twice — to establish this tikun forever. Sometimes <span class="h">chovlim</span> falling among <span class="h">n'imim</span> later overpower and damage — but now, through Eliyahu's great tikun, the tikun endures forever: the <span class="h">chovlim</span> transform into <span class="h">n'imim</span>. Twice <span class="v">"Hashem, He is <i>Elokim</i>"</span> — for the <span class="h">n'imim</span> and the <span class="h">chovlim</span> transformed into <span class="h">n'imim</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 4 — Why Called <i>"Minchah"</i>: <i>Tzedakah</i> as the Poor Man's Offering — for His <i>Kavod</i> Alone</div>

<div class="p">Why is this prayer called <span class="h">Minchah</span> (the <span class="h">Minchah</span> offering was also brought in the morning — the Tosafos' question)? Now, at <span class="h">Minchah</span>, we sweeten and repair the <span class="h">chovlim</span> — this tikun comes through <span class="h">tzedakah</span>. Therefore this prayer is called <span class="h">Minchah</span>: <span class="v">"those who bring <i>Minchah</i> in <i>tzedakah</i>."</span></div>

<div class="p">The essential tikun: <span class="h">tzedakah</span> in the aspect of a <span class="h">korban Minchah</span> — the poor man's offering, brought with his entire soul. Rashi on <span class="v">"a soul that brings a <i>Minchah</i> offering"</span>: in all offerings, <span class="v">"soul"</span> [<span class="h">nefesh</span>] is not stated except regarding the <span class="h">Minchah</span> — who customarily brings a <span class="h">Minchah</span>? A poor man. Hashem considers it as if he offered his soul. When the <span class="h">chovlim</span> overpower (damaging the <span class="h">n'imim</span> when falling among them), this happens because the vessel of <span class="h">tzedakah</span> is incomplete — not receiving the <span class="h">No'am</span>'s light fully, making it hard to repair the <span class="h">chovlim</span>. The essential cause: <span class="h">tzedakah</span> not fulfilled properly. <span class="h">Tzedakah</span>'s value is beyond measure — all Torah, all tikun of all worlds depends on it (all was created for His <span class="h">kavod</span>, and His <span class="h">kavod</span> is revealed through <span class="h">tzedakah</span>). Therefore <span class="mx">"<i>tzedakah</i> is equal to the entire Torah."</span></div>

<div class="p">One must give abundantly and pray to merit fulfilling <span class="h">tzedakah</span> properly — giving wholeheartedly for His Name's sake, to worthy poor who glorify His <span class="h">kavod</span>. Not for one's own honor, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span> — as happens when people give only to those with power and prestige (lest they lose their own honor), while ignoring worthy poor who study Torah in simplicity. Such <span class="h">tzedakah</span> (for self-honor) cannot fully repair the <span class="h">chovlim</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The essential tikun: <span class="h">tzedakah</span> in the aspect of the <span class="h">Minchah</span> (= the poor man's offering with intent for Heaven alone, as his offering is small). <span class="mx">"One who brings much and one who brings little — so long as he directs his heart to Heaven."</span> The poor man certainly intends for Heaven alone. So too the wealthy: however much he gives, he should consider it as the poor man's offering — for before Hashem, all are poor: <span class="mx">"who preceded Me?"</span> — <span class="v">"all is from You; from Your hand we have given You."</span> David HaMelech, when giving abundant wealth for the Bais HaMikdash, said: <span class="v">"in my poverty I have prepared for the House of Hashem — gold and silver."</span> He always called himself poor: <span class="v">"I am poor and destitute."</span> Such <span class="h">tzedakah</span> is exceedingly precious — considering himself poor, not intending for self-honor at all. This is <span class="h">Minchah</span>: <span class="v">"those who bring <i>Minchah</i> in <i>tzedakah</i>"</span> — receiving the <span class="h">No'am</span> fully, repairing the <span class="h">chovlim</span>. Since this tikun is needed especially at <span class="h">Minchah</span> time (the essential repair of the <span class="h">chovlim</span>), the prayer is called <span class="h">Minchah</span>. <span class="v">"How precious is Your <i>chesed</i>, O G-d"</span> — from which our Sages derived: not everyone who wishes to give <span class="h">tzedakah</span> properly can do so. <span class="v">"People shall take shelter in the shadow of Your wings"</span> — may one merit giving to people sheltering under His wings (truly worthy poor). Then the vessel is complete, receiving the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> — <span class="v">"they shall be sated from the abundance of Your house; from the stream of Your delights You shall give them drink."</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 5 — <i>Tefilas Arvis</i>: Yaakov, <i>Emes</i>, and the Tikun of All <i>Chovlim</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Tefilas Arvis</span> — established by Yaakov. Yaakov is the perfection of the Avos and the essential tikun of Adam HaRishon's sin (which damaged the <span class="h">chovlim</span>). Avraham began drawing the <span class="h">no'am</span> through abundant <span class="h">chesed</span> — establishing <span class="h">Shacharis</span>. Yitzchak sweetened the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (preventing them from damaging the <span class="h">n'imim</span>) — establishing <span class="h">Minchah</span>. Yaakov is the essential tikun — establishing <span class="h">Arvis</span>: praying even at night when darkness intensifies and <span class="h">chovlim</span> rule: <span class="v">"in it every beast of the forest creeps forth"</span> (= <span class="h">chovlim</span> and <span class="h">mazikim</span> [damagers]). All <span class="h">mazikim</span> are called <span class="h">m'chablim</span> [destroyers]; their power comes from sinful damage [<span class="h">chavalah</span>]: <span class="v">"we have dealt very corruptly"</span>; and especially flawed <span class="h">Bris</span> (the essential damage to the <span class="h">n'imim</span>). Their rule is at night: <span class="v">"nocturnal occurrence,"</span> <span class="h">Rachmana litzlan</span>.</div>

<div class="p">At night, by law, there is no obligation to pray (the <span class="h">mochin</span> of <span class="h">no'am</span> having fully withdrawn: <span class="mx">"when night spreads its wings over the world, all gates of Gan Eden are sealed"</span> [Zohar]). Yaakov, through his great power, established prayer even at night. Yaakov is the aspect of truth [<span class="h">emes</span>]: <span class="v">"grant truth to Yaakov."</span> Through <span class="h">emes</span>, all <span class="h">chovlim</span> (= <span class="h">machaloikes</span>) are nullified. Yitzchak began repairing the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (at day — <span class="h">Minchah</span>); Yaakov established <span class="h">Arvis</span> — praying even in total darkness. <span class="h">Emes</span> illuminates within the deepest darkness: <span class="v">"though I sit in darkness, Hashem is my light"</span>; <span class="v">"darkness is not dark to You; night shines as day"</span>; <span class="v">"though I walk through the valley of death's shadow, I fear no evil — for You are with me."</span></div>

<div class="p">Whoever desires truth is not harmed by <span class="h">machaloikes</span> — he believes that <span class="mx">"both these and these are the words of the Living G-d."</span> The Sages taught how to conduct oneself: doubtful Torah-law — stringent; doubtful Rabbinic-law — lenient; individual vs. majority — follow the majority. Even regarding disputes among <span class="h">tzadikim</span>: the one who desires truth receives a truthful angel and merits knowing the truth. How much more so when the disputants are coarse or wicked — the truth is visible.</div>

<div class="p">Yaakov merited the complete tikun of <span class="h">Bris</span>: <span class="v">"the first of my strength"</span> — he did not flaw the drawing of <span class="h">n'imim</span> for self-enjoyment at all. His bed was complete — no defective offspring (unlike Avraham from whom Yishmael came, and Yitzchak from whom Esav came — the essential <span class="h">chovlim</span> who destroyed the Bais HaMikdash and exiled Israel). Though the holy Avos labored greatly, exceedingly damaged <span class="h">chovlim</span> arose that could not yet be repaired — producing Esav and Yishmael. But Yaakov's bed was complete: all <span class="h">chovlim</span> seeking hold in him were repaired through his great <span class="h">emes</span>. He merited the holiness of Eretz Yisrael without boundary: <span class="v">"you shall burst forth to the west and east"</span> — an inheritance without borders. Avraham called the place of the Bais HaMikdash "mountain"; Yitzchak called it "field" (where <span class="h">chovlim</span> — wild beasts and <span class="h">mazikim</span> — rule; both Temples corresponding to them were destroyed). But Yaakov called it "house" — no hold for <span class="h">chovlim</span> there. The essential <span class="h">No'am</span> is in the Bais HaMikdash: the supreme holiness of Eretz Yisrael where <span class="h">halachah</span> is clarified (= <span class="mx">"they delight each other in <i>halachah</i>"</span>). The Sanhedrin sat there clarifying all <span class="h">halachos</span>: <span class="v">"you shall arise and ascend to the place."</span> <span class="v">"One thing I have asked... to dwell in the House of Hashem... to gaze upon the <i>no'am</i> of Hashem"</span> — in the House specifically. The essential third Bais HaMikdash, built through Yaakov's merit, will endure forever. Yaakov = the central bolt running from end to end — from the supreme <span class="h">No'am</span> (unblemished) downward to repair even the most damaged <span class="h">chovlim</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 6 — Yaakov's Vow: Stones' Dispute Resolved; Complete <i>Tzedakah</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He encountered the place"</span> — establishing <span class="h">Arvis</span>. <span class="v">"He took of the stones of the place and placed them at his head."</span> Our Sages: the stones quarreled with each other — then became one stone. The stones are the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (= <span class="h">machaloikes</span>, stumbling-stones: <span class="v">"if men quarrel and one strikes his fellow with a stone"</span>) — truly quarreling. Yaakov, through his great <span class="h">emes</span>, made peace among them — they became one stone. Therefore he then established <span class="h">Arvis</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Then <span class="v">"Yaakov vowed a vow"</span> — a generous-hearted gift: accepting the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">tzedakah</span> in completeness, tithing from everything. The essential tikun (drawing the <span class="h">no'am</span>) is through <span class="h">tzedakah</span> — in its completeness through Yaakov: <span class="v">"justice and <i>tzedakah</i> in Yaakov."</span> <span class="h">Ma'aser</span> [tithe] — repairing all Creation (made by Ten Utterances) through the ten aspects of the <span class="h">kavod</span>. <span class="v">"I shall surely tithe [<i>asair a'asrenu</i>] for You"</span> — "for You": his intent in tithing is solely to fulfill His will, not for self-honor. <span class="v">"<i>Tzedek tzedek</i> you shall pursue"</span> — intent in <span class="h">tzedakah</span> only for the sake of <span class="h">tzedek</span>. When <span class="h">tzedakah</span> is for self-honor — the <span class="h">chovlim</span> can damage the <span class="h">n'imim</span>: <span class="v">"the place of <i>tzedek</i> — there was wickedness."</span> But <span class="v">"<i>tzedek tzedek</i> you shall pursue"</span> — twice, because the <span class="h">chovlim</span> too are transformed into <span class="h">tzedek</span>. <span class="v">"So that you shall live and inherit the Land"</span> — meriting Eretz Yisrael where the <span class="h">No'am</span> flows. <span class="v">"You shall make known to me the path of life; joys before Your face; pleasantness at Your right hand forever"</span> — forever specifically, through Yaakov (= <span class="h">emes</span> = light of the face = <span class="v">"seekers of Your face — Yaakov, Selah"</span>). He merited eternal pleasantness — the third Bais HaMikdash enduring forever.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 7 — <i>Rosh HaShanah</i>: The <i>Shofar</i> Awakens the <i>No'am HaElyon</i></div>

<div class="p">On <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> the world was created — Adam HaRishon (= the essential purpose). His <span class="h">kavod</span> is through man; man is drawn from the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>. The <span class="h">No'am</span> must be drawn on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> — through the <span class="h">shofar</span> (= the totality of ten types of melody: <span class="v">"play well with the <i>teruah</i>"</span> = <span class="h">no'am</span> = <span class="v">"pleasant songster of Israel"</span>): <span class="v">"G-d ascended with the <i>teruah</i>; Hashem, with the sound of the <i>shofar</i> — sing to G-d, sing!"</span>. On <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> we read of the binding of Yitzchak — the first holy birth, drawn from the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>, the essential revelation of His <span class="h">kavod</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The intense judgments of <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> require many sweetenings. When the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> is aroused to reveal His <span class="h">kavod</span>, the <span class="h">chovlim</span> come to be repaired. Adam HaRishon's sin (which caused the <span class="h">chovlim</span>'s damage) was on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> — therefore all judgments are aroused then (<span class="h">chovlim</span> = <span class="h">machaloikes</span> = harsh judgments). The <span class="h">tzadikim</span>'s entire work on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> is to sweeten the judgments — preventing the <span class="h">chovlim</span> from damaging the <span class="h">n'imim</span>, ensuring the <span class="h">n'imim</span> repair the <span class="h">chovlim</span>. For this one must travel to the great <span class="h">tzadikim</span> on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> — they who know how to accomplish this tikun in completeness.</div>

<div class="p">We visit <span class="h">tzadikim</span>'s graves on <span class="h">Erev Rosh HaShanah</span> — the <span class="h">tzadik</span>'s passing was in the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>. The greater the light drawn from the <span class="h">No'am</span>, the more damaged <span class="h">chovlim</span> come to be repaired (and can cause greater damage). Therefore an exceedingly great <span class="h">tzadik</span> is needed — one who can draw from the ultimate <span class="h">No'am</span> without the slightest flaw (having purified himself from all worldly cravings absolutely, with no trace of desire). Only such a one can ascend to the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> to repair the <span class="h">chovlim</span>. He merits eternal pleasantness: <span class="v">"pleasantness at Your right hand forever"</span> — where no flaw reaches.</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">shofar</span> of <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> encompasses all ten types of melody (= the totality of supernal pleasantness). The <span class="h">shofar</span>'s sound is exceedingly powerful and lofty — ascending to arouse the ultimate <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> where all is repaired: <span class="v">"the sound of the <i>shofar</i> grew increasingly powerful"</span>; <span class="v">"the sound of the <i>shofar</i> was exceedingly powerful."</span> But the great <span class="h">tzadik</span>'s power is needed. Since such a <span class="h">tzadik</span> is not common now, we go to the graves of <span class="h">tzadikim</span> of supreme stature who merited this. <span class="v">"Fortunate is the people who know the <i>teruah</i>"</span> — <span class="h">yod'ai</span> specifically: they can arouse the <span class="h">mochin</span> through the <span class="h">teruah</span>, reaching the ultimate <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>. <span class="v">"Hashem, in the light of Your face they shall walk"</span>; <span class="v">"in Your Name they shall rejoice all day"</span> (= <span class="v">"seven joys..."</span>); <span class="v">"through Your <i>tzedakah</i> they shall be exalted"</span> — the essential tikun through <span class="h">tzedakah</span>. Therefore all Israel increase <span class="h">tzedakah</span> in these days — drawing the <span class="h">No'am</span> through the vessel of <span class="h">tzedakah</span>. This is the essential <span class="h">teshuvah</span> of <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> and the Ten Days of <span class="h">Teshuvah</span>: all sins derive from the <span class="h">chovlim</span> — now we repair them.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 8 — <i>Yom Kippur</i>: <i>Bris</i> of <i>No'am</i> and <i>Kavod</i>; Fasting and the Five Prayers</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Yom Kippur</span>: the ultimate completion of the tikun of all sins. Forgiveness of sins — on <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span> we ascend to <span class="h">Binah</span> (= the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>: <span class="h">No'am</span> = 161 in <span class="h">gematria</span>...). The holy fast of <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span> (five afflictions), preceded by obligatory eating on <span class="h">Erev Yom Kippur</span>: all Creation was for His <span class="h">kavod</span> — the essential <span class="h">kavod</span> through <span class="h">holadah</span> from the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>.</div>

<div class="p">All this world's pleasures and loves descend from the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>: <span class="v">"how beautiful and how pleasant — love among delights."</span> The <span class="h">tzadikim</span>'s entire work: not receiving this world's sweetness for themselves, but breaking all cravings and elevating all pleasantness to its source (= the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>). A Torah scholar is forbidden to fast excessively (our Sages) — Hashem desires the world's continuance, and one must draw the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> into this world's loves (eating, drinking) which sustain the world, standing in this test: not pursuing bitter worldly sweetness, but sanctifying oneself according to Torah, elevating pleasantness to its source — the essential <span class="h">kavod</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Yom Kippur</span> is the World to Come — no eating or drinking. <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span>: <span class="mx">"the <i>trin</i> [two] — mother and daughter ascend together"</span> (Zohar). Mother = <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span> (<span class="h">Binah</span>: <span class="v">"if you call <i>Binah</i> 'mother'"</span>). Daughter = <span class="h">kavod</span> (<span class="h">Malchus</span>: <span class="v">"all the <i>kavod</i> of the king's daughter"</span>). These are <span class="h">Naomi</span> and <span class="h">Rus</span>: <span class="h">Naomi</span> = <span class="h">No'am</span>; <span class="h">Rus</span> = <span class="h">kavod</span> (our Sages: "she was called <span class="h">Rus</span> because from her came David who <span class="h">rivah</span> [saturated] Hashem with songs and praises" = <span class="h">kavod</span>). In exile they walked together; on <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span> they ascend together — <span class="h">kavod</span> ascends to the <span class="h">No'am</span> without the garment of worldly loves. All is repaired: <span class="mx">"the Satan has no permission to accuse."</span> The <span class="h">chovlim</span>'s sustenance is nullified (coming only from flawed <span class="h">kavod</span> through damaged worldly pleasantness). But we cannot receive <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span>'s illumination without eating <span class="h">Erev Yom Kippur</span> — one cannot merit the World to Come without repairing oneself in this world. <span class="h">Erev Yom Kippur</span>: holy eating elevates His <span class="h">kavod</span> (<span class="mx">"the table of kings — the King of <i>Kavod</i>"</span>). Then on <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span>: elevating His <span class="h">kavod</span> through the five voices of the five prayers — from the <span class="h">No'am</span> without garments (mother and daughter ascending together).</div>

<div class="p"><i>[The author notes: these matters still need broader explanation, but from concern for forgetting them entirely, he records them as they are for now.]</i></div>

<div class="sn">§ 9 — <i>Sukkah</i>: Elevating This World's Pleasantness to the <i>No'am HaElyon</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Sukkah</span>: the essential <span class="h">mitzvah</span> is eating, drinking, and sleeping in the <span class="h">Sukkah</span> — bringing all human needs and pleasures inside. <span class="h">Sukkah</span> = <span class="mx">"the mother who shelters [<i>m'sakheches</i>] her children"</span> (= the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>, <span class="h">Binah</span>: <span class="v">"if you call <i>Binah</i> 'mother'"</span>). Through the holiness of <span class="h">Sukkah</span>, we elevate all pleasantness in eating and drinking to the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>. On <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span> we merited the World to Come (no garment of physicality — only the holy voices of the five prayers, five afflictions). But this is possible only for a limited time (<span class="h">Yom Kippur</span>; or fasts for <span class="h">teshuvah</span>). Man's essential service: eating and drinking according to Torah, not pursuing worldly sweetness, but connecting all to the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>. Even one who merely refrains from wine is called a sinner (for not elevating its pleasantness to its source). Therefore after <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span>, Hashem granted us the <span class="h">Sukkah</span> — <span class="mx">"shade of faith"</span> — drawing the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>'s light upon us, eating and drinking to connect all worldly pleasantness to its source.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 10 — <i>Shemini Atzeres</i> and <i>Simchas Torah</i>: The Ten Utterances Renewed</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Shemini Atzeres</span> and <span class="h">Simchas Torah</span>: we complete and begin the Torah; everyone receives the honor of <span class="h">aliyos</span> and is told: <span class="mx">"give honor to the Torah."</span> <span class="h">Shemini Atzeres</span> is the completion of the tikun begun on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> (the <span class="h">Nukvah</span> retains the "drop" for <span class="h">holadah</span>, as known). Then the essential <span class="h">kavod</span> is revealed — we begin <span class="h">Bereishis</span>, reading all Ten Utterances by which the world was created for His <span class="h">kavod</span>. Now, with the tikun of the <span class="h">No'am</span> complete (reaching <span class="h">holadah</span> of Jewish souls), the Ten Utterances shine with great light.</div>

<div class="p">We complete the Torah — ending with Moshe Rabbainu's great <span class="h">kavod</span>: <span class="v">"all the signs and wonders... the mighty hand and great awe"</span> — through which His <span class="h">kavod</span> was tremendously magnified: <span class="v">"I shall be honored through Pharaoh"</span>; <span class="v">"so that My Name be told throughout the earth."</span> This shines most on <span class="h">Shemini Atzeres</span> — the completion of all three <span class="h">Regalim</span> (from Pesach, all commemorating the Exodus where His <span class="h">kavod</span> was magnified). The essential tikun from <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> to <span class="h">Shemini Atzeres</span> repairs Adam HaRishon's sin (damaging the <span class="h">kavod</span>, enabling the <span class="h">chovlim</span>, as if destroying the world made by Ten Utterances). In His mercy, <span class="h">teshuvah</span> was granted; from Adam came the Avos and all Israel, who repair his sin each year from <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> to <span class="h">Shemini Atzeres</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Everyone is told <span class="mx">"give honor to the Torah"</span> — to warn everyone: do not take <span class="h">kavod</span> for yourself, return all <span class="h">kavod</span> to the Torah and to Hashem. The Ten Utterances' illumination comes through holy <span class="h">kavod</span> (= the root of Creation). The <span class="h">kavod</span> must be entirely an "utterance," entirely a "saying" (as explained in the above teaching) — when one does not benefit from the <span class="h">kavod</span> at all, returning it all to Hashem (= simple unity with the Torah). <span class="mx">"Give honor to the Torah."</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 11 — Moshe's Breaking the <i>Luchos</i>: Forgetting, <i>Machaloikes</i>, and the Tikun of <i>Chovlim</i></div>

<div class="p">Our Sages (cited by Rashi on <span class="v">"before the eyes of all Israel"</span>): Moshe was moved to break the <span class="h">Luchos</span> before their eyes — and Hashem agreed: <span class="mx">"well done that you broke them."</span> This is among Moshe's tremendous achievements. The Calf's sin was through the <span class="h">Erev Rav</span> — <span class="h">chovlim</span> that damaged the <span class="h">n'imim</span>. Moshe wanted to bring the <span class="h">Erev Rav</span> close (from Egypt, the ultimate contamination) — thinking the <span class="h">No'am</span> drawn at Sinai would repair them. But being too corrupt, they damaged even Israel. Seeing this, Moshe broke the <span class="h">Luchos</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Through breaking the <span class="h">Luchos</span>, forgetting entered the world — and from forgetting, <span class="h">machaloikes</span> in Israel (the holy <span class="h">machaloikes</span> of the <span class="h">Tanna'im</span> and <span class="h">Amora'im</span>): <span class="mx">"when the students of Shammai and Hillel who did not serve sufficiently increased, <i>machaloikes</i> increased"</span> (through forgetting from insufficient study). Our Sages say: the day <span class="h">machaloikes</span> arose was like the day the <span class="h">Luchos</span> were broken — all <span class="h">machaloikes</span> in holiness derives from the breaking.</div>

<div class="p">Through this very thing — a great tikun of the <span class="h">chovlim</span>. <span class="mx">"Judgment is sweetened only at its root"</span>: specifically through holy <span class="h">machaloikes</span> (from the <span class="h">Luchos</span>' breaking), the sustenance of the <span class="h">chovlim</span> (= <span class="h">machaloikes</span> of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>) is sweetened and nullified. Through holy <span class="h">machaloikes</span>, those whose <span class="h">mochin</span> are truly <span class="h">chovlim</span> are distanced — they who seek self-honor and would damage the <span class="h">n'imim</span>. Those who desire truth endure humiliation and approach — only through giving up self-honor (repairing the original flaw of <span class="h">kavod</span>). Without the forgetting and <span class="h">machaloikes</span>, everyone would run after the pleasantness of Torah (and many who seek self-honor would damage the <span class="h">n'imim</span>). But now — doubts, difficulties, and <span class="h">machaloikes</span> serve as a test: those who desire truth see it and approach through suffering, labor, and humiliation. Those who do not — distance themselves (and rightly so, lest they damage the <span class="h">n'imim</span>).</div>

<div class="p">Even after the forgetting and <span class="h">machaloikes</span> from the <span class="h">Luchos</span>' breaking, anyone who desires truth can still taste some of the Torah's pleasantness — even a small taste justifies casting away all cravings and honor. This is the way of the great <span class="h">tzadikim</span> even now: first revealing the Torah's pleasantness, then immediately concealing it and casting forgetting. This is: <span class="mx">"the <i>Luchos</i> and the broken <i>Luchos</i> rest in the Ark"</span> — the true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> draw Torah as both <span class="h">Luchos</span> and broken <span class="h">Luchos</span>: revealing, then concealing. All as a test — whoever desires truth will pursue it despite everything.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 12 — <i>Yom Tov Sheini Shel Galuyos</i>: Repair Through Doubt; Believing in All <i>Tzadikim</i></div>

<div class="p">In <span class="h">Chutz LaAretz</span>, the main joy of <span class="h">Yom Tov</span> is on the second day (observed due to doubt) — especially <span class="h">Simchas Torah</span>, which falls on the second day specifically. Outside the Land (where <span class="h">chovlim</span> take hold), the tikun is only possible through the aspect of doubts (= <span class="h">machaloikes</span>). On <span class="h">Yom Tov</span>, the <span class="h">No'am</span> flows (= the joy of <span class="h">Yom Tov</span>). One must ascend to the Bais HaMikdash (= Eretz Yisrael's supreme holiness, the essential <span class="h">No'am</span>). Outside the Land, the <span class="h">chovlim</span> are repaired through the second day of <span class="h">Yom Tov</span> (observed from doubt). This is the essential tikun — approaching from within <span class="h">machaloikes</span> and doubts, believing in all <span class="h">tzadikim</span> even though they dispute each other. Not like scoffers who say: "since they dispute, I reject both" — that borders on heresy. The truth: believe in all, ignoring the <span class="h">machaloikes</span> between them.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"If you do not know, O fairest among women, go forth in the footsteps of the flock, and tend your kids by the shepherds' tents"</span> — <span class="h">haro'im</span> [the shepherds], in the plural. Approach all of them — since you do not know whom to follow, approach all who guide according to the Torah as transmitted by our Sages in the Gemara, <span class="h">Poskim</span>, and <span class="h">sifrai yir'ah</span>. Only from those who deny, following paths of philosophical inquiry, seeking to deviate from Moshe's Torah, teaching external wisdoms, removing the yoke — from them one must distance absolutely. But all who lead according to Torah — <span class="v">"cling to Him"</span> = <span class="mx">"cling to Torah scholars."</span></div>

<div class="p">The second day of <span class="h">Yom Tov</span> (from doubt): just as we observe stringently from doubt, so we must approach all <span class="h">tzadikim</span> from doubt. In <span class="h">Chutz LaAretz</span>, the essential joy is on the second day — when the <span class="h">chovlim</span> are repaired through the <span class="h">n'imim</span>, His <span class="h">kavod</span> is magnified: <span class="mx">"when Yisro came..."</span> — great joy: <span class="v">"may Hashem's <i>kavod</i> endure forever; may Hashem rejoice in His works."</span> Even in Eretz Yisrael (where only one day is observed), <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> is two days even there — when the <span class="h">No'am</span> flows most, the most <span class="h">chovlim</span> come, requiring two days (from doubt) to repair them.</div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="mx">"once the witnesses were delayed and the Levites erred in the song — they decreed: witnesses of the new moon accepted only until <i>Minchah</i>."</span> Through flawed song (= <span class="h">no'am</span> = <span class="v">"pleasant songster of Israel"</span>) from the <span class="h">chovlim</span>'s damage — they decreed: only until <span class="h">Minchah</span> (the essential hold of <span class="h">chovlim</span>). If after <span class="h">Minchah</span> — two holy days. From this came the two days of <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> even in Eretz Yisrael.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 13 — Jealousy, Desire, and Honor Remove from the World</div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"Jealousy, desire, and honor remove a person from the world."</span> These three evil traits are the opposite of the holy aspects in the above teaching. <span class="h">Ta'avah</span> [desire] — the opposite of the holy <span class="h">No'am</span> (all cravings derive from the falling of the supernal sweetness). One must not pursue worldly sweetness but connect to the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>. Desire also diminishes <span class="h">tzedakah</span> (wanting to spend wealth on cravings, ignoring the poor) — the essential flaw of the <span class="h">No'am</span> (which flows through <span class="h">tzedakah</span>). <span class="h">Kavod</span> [honor-seeking] — the flaw of the holy <span class="h">kavod</span> (one must not pursue honor but return it to Hashem). <span class="h">Kinah</span> [jealousy] — jealousy, hatred, and <span class="h">machaloikes</span>, the opposite of <span class="h">shalom</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Each alone is terribly damaging — yet one might still have hope. But when they combine, they remove a person from the world entirely. Desire alone is harmful, but without honor-seeking, he would recognize his lowly place, nullify himself before the truly G-d-fearing, and be helped — <span class="mx">"whoever walks with the wise becomes wise."</span> But imaginary worldly honor deceives him — thinking he would lose honor by approaching the truly devout. He finds objections and distances himself. Worse — the Adversary stirs jealousy and hatred toward them and toward anyone touching his honor. Through all this he is driven from the world. If he would remove jealousy and hatred, approach the truly devout — they would teach him the straight and true path according to Torah, and he would merit a good end.</div>

<div class="p"><i>[Connected to the above teaching:]</i> <span class="v">"He shall carry a blessing from Hashem, and <i>tzedakah</i> from the G-d of his salvation. This is the generation of those who seek Him, who seek Your face — Yaakov, Selah."</span> Through <span class="h">tzedakah</span>, blessing and abundance are drawn from the <span class="h">No'am HaElyon</span>. <span class="v">"This is the generation of those who seek Him"</span> — all generations drawn through this. <span class="v">"Who seek Your face — Yaakov"</span> = <span class="v">"joys before Your face; pleasantness"</span> — Yaakov merited this most (his bed was complete — from him all Israel for all generations: <span class="v">"this is the generation..."</span>). <span class="v">"Lift up your heads, O gates... and the King of <i>Kavod</i> shall enter"</span> — His <span class="h">kavod</span> magnified. Mentioned twice — for the <span class="h">n'imim</span> and the <span class="h">chovlim</span> repaired by them (through both, His <span class="h">kavod</span> grows). This <span class="h">Mizmor</span> begins with Eretz Yisrael and <span class="h">Chutz LaAretz</span>: <span class="v">"the earth is Hashem's"</span> (= Eretz Yisrael); <span class="v">"the world and those who dwell in it"</span> (= <span class="h">Chutz LaAretz</span>) — the <span class="h">mochin</span> of outside the Land needing repair through the <span class="h">mochin</span> of Eretz Yisrael. All connected beautifully — therefore we say this <span class="h">Mizmor</span> at the entry of <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span>.</div>

<div class="cn">✦ End of Hilchos Tefilas HaMinchah, Halachah 6 (§§ 1–13) ✦<br><i>Na Nach Nachma Nachman May'Uman</i></div>

